Colour the scroll bars of the GTK sheets from the slider settings

The scroll bar rules of the GTK sheets stated one case of the Qt
style. The thumb took the button ladder under every slider key,
and its gradient took the appearance key in place of the
sliderAppearance key. The trough took the window ladder, and no
groove path of the style reads that ladder.

Writer::scrollBar() now reads scrollSpec(). The helper states the
ladder of Style::sliderColors() under each slider key. It takes
one highlight step of that ladder for the pointer, and step two
of the Base ladder for the groove. Each border takes the border
step of the ladder of its fill. The style passes one colour array
to the fill and to the border of a box. A thumb tone that follows
no colour name gives a literal under the -fixed suffix, which
assert-pairs.sh and assert-paths.sh read. The ground of the bar
keeps the window rule, because the style paints no ground of its
own under the shipped keys.

assert-scrollbar.sh binds the widget rules to the settings over
fifteen arms and thirteen controls. The gradient arm of the
checks loses the glass stops of its thumb, because its settings
file sets no sliderAppearance key.

The change sits on the branch work/gtk4-theme of the local tree, as the
fourteenth commit. The fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !15
on system/qtcurve holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

